    "[risk] Browser presets and PDF export use startLocalHttpServer, which binds IPv4 loopback asynchronously. Core retains the synchronous startHttpServer API for existing callers; changing that API to asynchronous startup would break callers. Both reject lexical path traversal while preserving intentional asset symlinks. This is a static asset boundary, not a harness/submission OS privilege boundary.",
    "[risk] The requested migration targets macOS and Linux judging hosts. Windows compatibility is outside the requested scope; do not add Windows-specific code. Existing untouched Windows branches in core helpers do not expand this migration requirement.",
    "[risk] This library is not an OS sandbox. The judge deployment runs the entire harness and learner program as the same request sandbox user; server credentials remain in the privileged server process. Callers supply process isolation for untrusted programs. Preventing learners from reading model answers or their own request files is outside the security policy; do not add a harness/submission privilege split or symlink containment between them. Serving links does not grant filesystem permissions beyond the caller's OS user. Temporary asset assembly must nevertheless leave source files and linked directories unchanged.",
    "[risk] The HTML comparison preset retains the existing course harness contract: pixel equality of deterministic pages. It disables CSS animations and transitions and waits for fonts, but does not freeze JavaScript timers, randomness, or animated image frames. Dynamic exercises must use custom browser checks.",
    "[risk] HTML served-directory assembly treats source files and symlinks as complete overrides; a directory symlink overrides its whole subtree. Only actual source directories are merged into temporary directories, so shared assets never get written into linked source targets.",
    "[risk] Isolated judging copies only the problem directory. Ancestor asset lookup serves model-answer and submission subdirectories within it; shared course-level assets must be included inside each problem that requires them.",
    "[risk] Process termination cleanup is owned by the host: it provides and removes a per-run TMPDIR. Isolated CLI checks establish TMPDIR under their parent-owned temporary root; Judge supplies its own request scratch directory. Browser directory helpers provide normal async disposal and leave signal handling to the host, including graceful asynchronous shutdown. Direct library callers must own cleanup when disposal is interrupted.",
    "[risk] JavaScript course presets retain the existing console-idle heuristics and test-case conventions. The host bounds the entire harness process, including submissions that emit output indefinitely; per-operation Playwright timeouts are not an overall JavaScript execution deadline.",
    "[risk] Tomcat course grading requires an exclusive host slot for port 59000, the judge application name, GNU timeout/time, Maven offline dependencies, and CATALINA_HOME. The request host owns interrupted process and scratch-directory cleanup; this preset is not a concurrent Tomcat service manager.",
    "[risk] Tomcat startup must leave its Java server running after startup.sh returns. The synchronous Tomcat command runner preserves that lifecycle; the submission runner spawnWithLimits kills the entire subprocess group on child exit and cannot replace Tomcat startup without terminating its server.",
    "[risk] Spring Boot course grading requires Java, offline Maven dependencies, Bun, and an exclusive host slot for port 59000. The host owns interrupted subprocess and temporary-directory cleanup; the preset preserves the existing course build/startup/evaluation limits and verdict conventions, and is not a concurrent application supervisor.",
    "[risk] Browser presets sanitize embedded diagnostic text while preserving rejected error identity and process ownership. Explicit FORCE_COLOR=1 asks Bun to color its own uncaught-error rendering even for plain Error messages; the library must not change global color settings, swallow rejections, or take over process stderr to override that runtime policy. Without forced runtime color, the actual uncaught browser timeout CLI emits plain diagnostics after sanitization.",
